# Deliberately near-empty. Its mere PRESENCE stops npm from falling back to
# .gitignore for `npm pack`/`npm publish` filtering (npm's documented
# behavior: "if there is no .npmignore file, but a .gitignore file exists,
# its contents are used instead"). That fallback would otherwise silently
# strip `src/web/generated/**` and `src/web/frontend/fonts.generated.css`
# from the published tarball — both are gitignored build output (this repo's
# dev convention), but they are NOT optional for a package installed via
# `npm i -g slopwork`/`npx slopwork`: bin/slop.mjs runs `bun src/cli/index.ts`
# straight from the published `src/` (see that file's doc comment), and
# `src/web/server.ts` statically imports the generated SPA bundle — so
# `slop web` needs those files physically present in the published package.
# `prepublishOnly` (package.json) runs `bun run build:web` before every
# publish so they exist on disk when this file's (lack of) rules are
# evaluated. The `files` allowlist in package.json is what actually scopes
# the published tarball otherwise (node_modules/, tests/, dist/, etc. are
# simply never listed there); this file has nothing further to exclude.
